<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_Warscar.xml                   UtinniPatches — new file, SCARLANDS_STANDALONE_MOD_1
  ============================================================================

  Wires the ten remaining live-roster rows of the frozen twin's own
  RUT_Scarlands.xml (see that file's <wildAnimals>, MEASURED fresh this pass —
  it has moved on since SCARLANDS_STANDALONE_MOD_1's own analysis, which
  predates COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1's RUT_MortuaryCrawler wiring) into
  src/RimMandrake/Scarlands' RM_Warscar.xml, exactly as that mod's own three
  non-Star-Wars, non-RimUtinni donor rows (AA_SpinedGow, RG_Rimclaw,
  AA_Helixien) already ship inline there.

  WHY THESE TEN GO THROUGH A PATCH, NOT THE BIOME DEF DIRECTLY: an RM-tier def
  may not name RimStarWars- or RimUtinni-tier content by defName (Q11a,
  biome_mod_architecture.md §7) — doing so would make the "franchise/
  campaign-free" mod hard-depend on Star Wars or campaign content. Same shape
  every other split biome's Star-Wars-fauna routing uses (see
  WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml, WildAnimals_Greentide.xml, WildAnimals_CrackedLands.xml).

  ROSTER (all ten, MEASURED against the live RUT_Scarlands.xml, not the stale
  item analysis):

  🔴 MLIE_ABSORPTION_BIOME_WIRING_1 (2026-09-25): the swap flagged below as
  "not this item's scope" is now done — Mynock retargeted to our own
  RSW_Mynock (mandrake.rsw.swbestiary), joining the other RSW_ ports below.
  This file no longer casts any bare mlie.starwarsanimalcollection defName.

  who.vfee.isopodageneline (weapon-descendant insects):
    SW_Electrictick        0.3
    SW_Electricgryllotalpa 0.15
    SW_Juggernautbeetles   0.05

  mandrake.rsw.swbestiary (our own Star Wars-tier ports):
    RSW_CrystalFairyMole   0.5
    RSW_MegaphoridLarva    0.5
    RSW_FoundryBeetle      0.18
    RSW_Korrum             0.05  (deliberately NOT the roster's 0.5 —
                                 ECOSYSTEM_PYRAMID_LAW_1, do not "fix" this)

  RUT_ScarRoach and RUT_MortuaryCrawler are no longer cast here: WARSCAR_FREE_TIER_BODY_1
  moved them into mandrake.rm.warscar as RM_ScarRoach and RM_Pallbearer, listed inline in
  RM_Warscar.xml.

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing (PatchOperationConditional
  returns true on no match) — validate with
  skills/rimworld-modding/scripts/validate_patch.py against the live def dump
  before trusting these two blocks fired.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="who.vfee.isopodageneline">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Warscar"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Warscar"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <SW_Electrictick>0.3</SW_Electrictick>
        <SW_Electricgryllotalpa>0.15</SW_Electricgryllotalpa>
        <SW_Juggernautbeetles>0.05</SW_Juggernautbeetles>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Warscar"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Warscar"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <value>
        <RSW_Mynock>0.5</RSW_Mynock>
        <RSW_CrystalFairyMole>0.5</RSW_CrystalFairyMole>
        <RSW_MegaphoridLarva>0.5</RSW_MegaphoridLarva>
        <RSW_FoundryBeetle>0.18</RSW_FoundryBeetle>
        <RSW_Korrum>0.05</RSW_Korrum>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
